From 60e0ca36c55d2df3b651f28eeb09f78ccee10c3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:37:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06914/11362] [outer-loop] g50t: L6 first attempt, honest null
 with real progress

Round-8 gpt-5.6-sol session made the first-ever attempt at fresh L6
territory. L6 introduces an autonomous runner that advances one step
per successful player move (blocked actions don't advance it) on a
hidden track, bouncing back and forth. Two color-8 plates hold gates
open that would otherwise crush the runner if closed on it. Mapped and
validated a minimal stable two-holder solution (two committed clones
parking on the plates) that lets the runner cross both gates cleanly.

The runner's bouncing makes downstream color-11 toggles
phase-sensitive -- it re-closes what it opens on its return pass, so
player traversal must be timed to the runner's position, not just
convenience. The final synchronization attempt failed because blocked
wait-moves don't advance the runner, so an open window had already
closed by the time the player arrived.

Independently re-verified by the outer loop: the full 291-action
sequence replays cleanly from a fresh env.reset() to level=5,
state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED via the correct resolver-registered
apply function, matching the session's own report exactly. No new
level banked; frontier stays at level 5. Next attempt should apply the
now-solved two-holder technique directly and focus on timing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
